      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Awareness by medical practitioners of the need to keep their patients adequately informed of their conditions is of paramount importance in caring for those people who have had a myocardial infarction. This includes a realization that these people have questions to be answered at all stages of the illness, from the initial contact when in pain, throughout the hospital admission, and during rehabilitation."},
